{"qid":"Q1108445","names":["Kievan Rus'"],"title":"Kievan Rus'","endonym":{"native":"Рѹсь","lang":"Old East Slavic","roman":"Rusĭ"},"endonymWikidata":{"p1705":["рѹсьскаѧ землѧ (mis)"],"p1448":[]},"capsule":"The river-road federation of East Slavic principalities under the princes of Kiev, Christianized from Byzantium in 988. After Yaroslav the Wise it fragmented among rival branches of the Rurikid house, and the Mongol storm of 1237–1240 destroyed Kiev and subjected the lands to the Golden Horde.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases (Times Atlas of World History; Kinder & Hilgemann; Shepherd 1926) at ~0.07° resolution. \"Boundaries\" of Rus' were zones of tribute over forest peoples, not lines; northern and eastern extents are schematic. Confidence: low–moderate, core river towns excepted.","citations":[{"label":"Franklin & Shepard, The Emergence of Rus 750–1200 (Routledge)","url":"https://www.routledge.com/The-Emergence-of-Rus-750-1200/Franklin-Shepard/p/book/9780582490918"},{"label":"Russian Primary Chronicle (Cross trans., archive.org)","url":"https://archive.org/details/russianprimarych00cros"},{"label":"Britannica","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Kievan-Rus"}],"britannica":"topic/Kievan-Rus","wikipedia":"Kievan Rus'","positions":["Q26943762"],"rulers":[{"qid":"Q14974","name":"Vladimir the Great","start":980,"end":1015,"ordinal":null,"image":"Vladimir I of Kiev.PNG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Vladimir%20I%20of%20Kiev.PNG?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Anonymous illumination","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Владимир Святославич","nativeLang":"ru"},{"qid":"Q311575","name":"Sviatopolk I of Kiev","start":1015,"end":1016,"ordinal":null,"image":"Печать князя Ярополчича.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%87%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%8C%20%